{
    "background_story": "Jadiel was a young man from a small village in the mountains. He had always been rooted in his community, helping his family with their farm and participating in local traditions. However, when a devastating landslide destroyed their home and crops, Jadiel's family was forced to uproot their lives and move to the city. Jadiel struggled to adapt to the urban jungle, feeling lost and disconnected from his heritage. But as he began to explore the city, he discovered a vibrant community of artists and musicians who shared his passion for storytelling. Jadiel found solace in their company and began to create music that reflected his experiences, weaving together the old and the new. As he performed on street corners and in local cafes, he slowly began to rebuild his sense of identity and find a new sense of belonging.",
